"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[654],{4746(e,r,o){o.r(r),o.d(r,{_pageData:()=>t,default:()=>i});var a=o(641);const t=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-pre-order/pre-order-management.html","title":"Pre-Order Management (Admin Dashboard)","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-pre-order/pre-order-management.md"}'),s={name:"pre-order-management.md"},i=(0,o(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,r,o,t,s,i){return(0,a.uX)(),(0,a.CE)("div",null,[...r[0]||(r[0]=[(0,a.Fv)('<h1 id="pre-order-management-admin-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#pre-order-management-admin-dashboard"><span>Pre-Order Management (Admin Dashboard)</span></a></h1><p>Store administrators manage pre-order configurations, track customer pre-orders, check waitlists, reply to shopper inquiries, and manually create pre-orders through a central admin dashboard.</p><p>Access this workspace by navigating to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> in your WordPress sidebar.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-administrative-workspace-tabs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-administrative-workspace-tabs"><span>1. Administrative Workspace Tabs</span></a></h2><p>The dashboard is structured into seven tabs to separate key workflows:</p><h3 id="a-pre-order-products" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#a-pre-order-products"><span>A. Pre Order Products</span></a></h3><p>Lists all WooCommerce products and variations currently configured for pre-orders.</p><ul><li><strong>Information Displayed:</strong> Product title, SKU, base price, payment model (Full/Deposit), pre-order price/deposit, quantity limit, availability date, status (Enabled/Disabled).</li><li><strong>Inline Actions:</strong> Toggle Status (Enable/Disable), Edit configuration, Delete.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-pre-order-products-list.png" alt="Pre-Order Products List"></p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/pre-order-product-configuration.png" alt="Individual Product Pre-Order Configuration Panel"></p><h3 id="b-pre-order-list" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#b-pre-order-list"><span>B. Pre Order List</span></a></h3><p>Tracks every individual pre-order transaction placed by customers.</p><ul><li><strong>Information Displayed:</strong><ul><li><strong>Order ID:</strong> The parent WooCommerce order ID.</li><li><strong>Customer:</strong> Customer name or guest email.</li><li><strong>Pre-ordered Product:</strong> Title of the item.</li><li><strong>Quantity:</strong> Quantity ordered.</li><li><strong>Remaining Amount:</strong> Outstanding balance (zero for full payments).</li><li><strong>Linked Order:</strong> The secondary order ID created for balance payment.</li><li><strong>Status:</strong> <em>Pending</em>, <em>Notified</em>, <em>Completed</em>, or <em>Cancelled</em>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Actions:</strong> Send manual balance payment email alerts, cancel order, filter by pre-order status, or search by Order ID.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-preorder-placed-list.png" alt="Admin Pre-Orders Placed Table"></p><h3 id="c-campaigns" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#c-campaigns"><span>C. Campaigns</span></a></h3><p>Displays active promotional countdown campaigns scheduled for future releases.</p><ul><li><strong>Information Displayed:</strong> Product name, start date, end date, campaign status, countdown styling.</li><li><strong>Actions:</strong> Add new campaign, edit, delete, or activate.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-campaigns-list.png" alt="Admin Campaigns List"></p><h3 id="d-stock-subscribers-waitlist" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#d-stock-subscribers-waitlist"><span>D. Stock Subscribers (Waitlist)</span></a></h3><p>Tracks shoppers waiting for standard out-of-stock products to be restocked.</p><ul><li><strong>Information Displayed:</strong> Product name, subscriber name, email address, registration date, notification status.</li><li><strong>Actions:</strong> Filter by notification status, or delete subscriber.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-subscribers-list.png" alt="Admin Waitlist Subscribers Table"></p><h3 id="e-enquiries" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#e-enquiries"><span>E. Enquiries</span></a></h3><p>A dedicated support channel for customer queries regarding pre-order items.</p><ul><li><strong>Information Displayed:</strong> Enquiry ID, Customer email, Subject, Date, Status (Replied/Pending).</li><li><strong>Actions:</strong> Click <strong>View</strong> to open the threaded message panel and send replies directly from the dashboard.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-enquiries-list.png" alt="Admin Enquiries Dashboard"></p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-reply-thread.png" alt="Admin Reply Thread Panel"></p><h3 id="f-reports" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#f-reports"><span>F. Reports</span></a></h3><p>Provides sales charts and analytical metrics on pre-order campaigns, conversion rates, deposits pending, and total pre-order revenue.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-reports.png" alt="Admin Reports Dashboard"></p><hr><h2 id="_2-manual-pre-order-creation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-manual-pre-order-creation"><span>2. Manual Pre-Order Creation</span></a></h2><p>Administrators can manually create a pre-order on behalf of customers (e.g., for phone orders, wholesale clients, or manual overrides).</p><h3 id="step-by-step-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-by-step-workflow"><span>Step-by-Step Workflow</span></a></h3><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> and click the <strong>Add Pre-Order</strong> button at the top of the page.</li><li><strong>Select Customer:</strong><ul><li>For registered customers: Search and select their WordPress user account.</li><li>For guest shoppers: Enter the customer&#39;s billing email address.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Choose Product:</strong> Choose any product currently configured with active pre-order status.</li><li><strong>Configure Details:</strong><ul><li><strong>Quantity:</strong> Specify the number of items.</li><li><strong>Price Mode:</strong> Choose whether to charge the configured deposit (partial payment) or the full product price.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Submit Form:</strong><ul><li>Clicking <strong>Create Order</strong> creates a WooCommerce order containing the pre-order item.</li><li>The system sets the order status to <em>Pending Payment</em>, records pre-order tags, and lists the transaction in the <strong>Pre Order List</strong> with the remaining balance calculated.</li></ul></li><li>An invoice is automatically emailed to the customer with checkout instructions.</li></ol><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-manual-preorder-creation.png" alt="Manual Pre-Order Creation Form"></p><hr><h2 id="_3-product-release-restocking-workflows" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-product-release-restocking-workflows"><span>3. Product Release &amp; Restocking Workflows</span></a></h2><p>When a pre-ordered product becomes available, store owners initiate the release workflow:</p><h3 id="how-to-release-pre-ordered-products" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-release-pre-ordered-products"><span>How to Release Pre-Ordered Products</span></a></h3><ol><li><strong>Automatic Release:</strong> Go to <strong>Products</strong>, select the item, and change the stock status to <code>In Stock</code>. The system automatically triggers release tasks.</li><li><strong>Manual Release:</strong> Turn off the <strong>Pre-Order Status</strong> toggle under the product’s Pre-Order configuration tab. This immediately releases all associated pre-orders.</li></ol><h3 id="processing-payments" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#processing-payments"><span>Processing Payments</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Stripe Auto-Charge:</strong> If active, the system automatically bills the saved card in background batches of 20. If successful, the pre-order updates to <strong>Completed</strong>.</li><li><strong>Manual Billing:</strong> For other payment options or failed card payments, the system automatically emails the customer an invoice containing a link. The customer has a configured completion window (e.g., 7 days) to pay before the order is flagged.</li></ul>',44)])])}]])}}]);